  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Simplify the expression $[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ]^{10}.$",
  "worked_solution": "De Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\phi )]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=10$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ]^{10}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(10\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(10\\theta ).\n$$",
